# `next` is read behind `&&`: not every turn passes there. In a typed copy no guess is opened in a turn: what is not asked in front leaves the copy for good. Beside `row`, which every turn reads, `next` is asked the same test in front, and stays among the lists tested there: all four reads stand under proven lists.
